<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  QBX-246: the testkit's seams address the root their path names, so a .qxa can
  see inside an arrangement tab. Until they did, QBX-230, 231, 232, 233 and 234
  each had to be found by a human clicking something that did nothing.

  WHICH ARMS BITE, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Both arms below were watched
  failing on a deliberately sabotaged build, and the first draft of this header
  had them the wrong way round:

    1. THE COUNTS DIFFER, and this one gates the <assertions> block. The master
       has one lane, the arrangement two. Sabotaging SActionRunner to ignore
       root= fails the case with "assert-track-count: expected 2, got 1". This
       is the headline seam: the trailing <assertions> block EVERY case ends
       with, which could only ever see the master, and so the reason the whole
       family could not be gated.

    2. A QUALIFIED PATH REACHES THE ARRANGEMENT. Reverting the shell's seams to
       the pre-QBX-246 spelling (rootContainer() plus a bare stringToPath())
       fails the three Drums:1 lines below.

  WHY IT FAILS THERE, which is NOT the story told in QBX-242 and
  check_pathroot.py. Proposal 45 D9 hardened stringToPath: an unparsable
  component becomes SPATH_INVALID, not 0, and resolveByPath returns nullptr on
  it. So a bare parse of "Drums:1" does NOT become the master's lane 1 and does
  NOT resolve the wrong object. It FAILS CLOSED, and the seam answers nothing.
  The defect is a dead seam, not a seam reading the wrong tree.

  That is also why the Nope:0 lines, which look like the obvious gate, pass on
  BOTH builds and are kept only to pin the refusal: an unknown root must
  resolve to nothing, and since D9 a bare parse refuses it too, so the two
  defences agree and neither is isolated by this case. Saying so is the point.
  The wrong-tree half of the class is real but lives on the ROOT-RESOLUTION
  side, where a BARE path like "0" is resolved against the master while the
  object sits in an arrangement, and index {0} exists in every root.

  There is no positive per-track arm: the section-collapse state is a PROJECT
  property (SProjectProps::TrackDetail*Collapsed), not a per-track one, so no
  field of describeTrackDetailSections() differs between the master's lane and
  the arrangement's.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="arrangement_seams_see_the_root">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <!-- Deliberately confusable, as arrangement_verbs_scoped.qxa builds it:
         both roots carry a lane at index 0. The COUNTS are what differ. -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <set-track-name trackPath="0" name="MasterLane"/>

    <create-arrangement name="Drums"/>
    <add-track arrangement="Drums" index="-1"/>
    <add-track arrangement="Drums" index="-1"/>
    <set-track-name trackPath="Drums:0" name="DrumLane"/>
    <set-track-name trackPath="Drums:1" name="DrumLaneTwo"/>

    <!-- The action verb assert-track-count has been root-aware all along;
         stating it here pins the fixture that the <assertions> block reads. -->
    <assert-track-count arrangement="" count="1"/>
    <assert-track-count arrangement="Drums" count="2"/>

    <!-- ==== arm 2: a qualified path REACHES the arrangement's lane =====
         These are what fail when the seams go back to rootContainer() plus a
         bare parse: since proposal 45 D9 that parse fails closed, so the seam
         answers nothing at all. Drums:1 is an index the master does not even
         have, which is the point. -->
    <assert-track-detail-sections trackPath="Drums:1" contains="plugins="/>
    <assert-track-detail-layout trackPath="Drums:1" contains="w="/>
    <assert-ui-fonts trackPath="Drums:1" contains="small="/>

    <!-- ==== the refusal, pinned but NOT isolated (passes either way) ====
         An unknown root must resolve to nothing, never to the master's lane 0.
         Two defences give that answer today (rootNamed fails closed, and so
         does the D9 parse), so this gates the property without separating
         them. It is here so that losing BOTH is noticed. -->
    <assert-track-detail-sections trackPath="Nope:0" contains="plugins="
                                  expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-track-detail-layout trackPath="Nope:0" contains="w="
                                expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-ui-fonts trackPath="Nope:0" contains="small="
                     expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- and a refusal changes nothing in the master -->
    <assert-track-name trackPath="0" name="MasterLane"/>
  </actions>

  <!-- ==== arm 1: the headline seam, and the counts differ ============
       An absent root= is the master (one lane); root="Drums" is the
       arrangement (two). A runner that ignores root= reads the master twice
       and fails the second with "expected 2, got 1". -->
  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
    <assert-track-count root="Drums" equals="2"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
